      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(\\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)!}\\), let's start by simplifying the expression step-by-step.\n\n1. Recall the definition of factorial:\n   \\[\n   (N+1)! = (N+1) \\cdot N!\n   \\]\n\n2. Substitute \\((N+1)!\\) in the original expression:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1)!} = \\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1) \\cdot N!}\n   \\]\n\n3. Notice that \\((N-1)!\\) in the numerator and the denominator cancel each other out:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(N-1)!(N)}{(N+1) \\cdot N!} = \\frac{N}{(N+1)}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of the given expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{N}{N+1}}\n\\]",
